{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 32, "timestamp": 0, "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color", "SHELL": "/bin/bash"}, "title": "blind-tdd plugin demo"}
[0.35, "o", "\u001b[1mblind-tdd plugin — demo\u001b[0m  \u001b[2m(scratch: /tmp/tmp.GAXTRPd5kT)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.7, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.05, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[36m== 1. The blind writer tries to read the implementation ==\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.4, "o", "\u001b[2m# Claude Code sends this PreToolUse event to the path-guard hook:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.75, "o", "[blind-tdd] BLOCKED: Read access to 'src/calculator.py' denied by blind-TDD policy (path matches blocked pattern 'src/**'). Session: demo-writer, role: test_writer. Blind agents must not read implementation code; rely only on the task spec, acceptance_criteria, public_api.md, and external docs.\r\n"]
[3.0, "o", "\u001b[31m\u001b[1m-> hook exit 2 (2 = BLOCKED): the writer cannot see the code.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.25, "o", "\r\n"]
[4.6, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[36m== 2. The same writer reads its allowed spec surface ==\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.85, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[1m-> hook exit 0 (0 = allowed): public_api.md is on the whitelist.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[7.1, "o", "\r\n"]
[7.45, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[36m== 3a. RED — writer authors a failing test from the spec alone ==\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.7, "o", "\u001b[2m# Run the test before any implementation is importable:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.05, "o", "\u001b[31m\u001b[1m-> tests FAIL (RED): no implementation yet, as required.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.3, "o", "\r\n"]
[10.65, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[36m== 3b. SEAL — fingerprint the test with SHA-256 before code exists ==\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[11.0, "o", "sealed tests/test_calculator.py -> \u001b[2msha256:8d688ee5ad668cf4...\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[11.35, "o", "\r\n"]
[11.7, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[36m== 3c. GREEN — implementer writes code; the sealed test goes green ==\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[12.95, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[1m-> tests PASS (GREEN): the sealed AC-1 test is satisfied.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[14.2, "o", "\r\n"]
[14.55, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[36m== 4a. The implementer tries to edit the hash-locked test — BLOCKED ==\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[15.8, "o", "\u001b[2m# A runner/implementer role editing a locked test hits the path-guard:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.15, "o", "[blind-tdd] BLOCKED: Edit access to 'tests/test_calculator.py' denied by blind-TDD policy (write to hash-locked test file (red_state)). Session: demo-runner, role: test_runner. Blind agents must not read implementation code; rely only on the task spec, acceptance_criteria, public_api.md, and external docs.\r\n"]
[17.4, "o", "\u001b[31m\u001b[1m-> hook exit 2 (2 = BLOCKED): a sealed test cannot be edited in-band.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[18.65, "o", "\r\n"]
[19.0, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[36m== 4b. Even a tamper through the shell breaks the seal ==\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[19.35, "o", "\u001b[2m# Suppose a test is changed anyway (e.g. weakened to assert nothing):\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[19.7, "o", "sealed:  \u001b[2m8d688ee5ad668cf4...\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[20.05, "o", "current: \u001b[2m716713f51b4e4f6e...\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[20.4, "o", "\u001b[31m\u001b[1m-> SHA-256 mismatch: the runner fails the gate regardless of the result.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[21.65, "o", "\r\n"]
[22.0, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[32mDemo complete.\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlindness, the seal, and the lock are enforced by the shipped hooks.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
